__pycache__/
*.pyc

# This repo ships the TOOL — bin/, canon/, schemas/, templates/, adapters/, tests/.
# It does NOT commit a self-adoption. `socom adopt` materializes the substrate and
# the runtime adapters per-clone; they are generated build output, never source.
/.socom/
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
# CONTENTS, not the directory: git cannot re-include a path whose parent dir is
# excluded, so `/.claude/` would swallow the negation below without a word.
/.claude/*
# …except hand-authored skills, which are SOURCE, not generated adoption. The
# rule above exists to keep `socom adopt`'s output (agents/, settings.json) out
# of the repo that ships the tool; it must not also swallow the workflow
# substrate this repo is worked WITH.
!/.claude/skills/
/.cursor/
/.githooks/
/.gitlab-ci.yml
/.github/workflows/socom-gates.yml
